---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Base title="Vital Signs Ranges" activeSlug="vital-signs">
  <div class="breadcrumb"><a href={base}>MedKit</a> / References / <span>Vital Signs Ranges</span></div>
  <h1>Vital Signs Ranges</h1>
  <p class="cat-desc">Normal ranges for heart rate, blood pressure, respiratory rate, SpO₂ and temperature by age.</p>

  <div class="article" style="margin-top:18px">
    <p>Reference ranges are approximate and vary between sources and clinical context. Use as a screening aid, not a diagnostic threshold.</p>

    <h2>Adults (≥ 18 yr)</h2>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Vital</th><th>Normal range</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Heart rate</td><td>60–100 bpm</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Blood pressure</td><td>&lt; 120 / &lt; 80 mmHg</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Respiratory rate</td><td>12–20 / min</td></tr>
      <tr><td>SpO₂</td><td>≥ 95%</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Temperature</td><td>36.1–37.2 °C</td></tr>
    </table>

    <h2>Children (1–12 yr)</h2>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Vital</th><th>Normal range</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Heart rate</td><td>70–120 bpm</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Respiratory rate</td><td>18–30 / min</td></tr>
      <tr><td>SpO₂</td><td>≥ 95%</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Temperature</td><td>36.4–37.5 °C</td></tr>
    </table>

    <h2>Infants (&lt; 1 yr)</h2>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Vital</th><th>Normal range</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Heart rate</td><td>100–160 bpm</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Respiratory rate</td><td>30–60 / min</td></tr>
      <tr><td>SpO₂</td><td>≥ 95%</td></tr>
    </table>

    <h3>FAQ</h3>
    <details class="faq"><summary>When is tachycardia concerning?</summary><div class="body">A resting HR above the age range can reflect fever, pain, dehydration, anaemia, hypoxia or cardiac causes. Correlate with the clinical picture.</div></details>
    <details class="faq"><summary>What SpO₂ is too low?</summary><div class="body">Sustained &lt; 92% generally warrants escalation; &lt; 90% is a red flag. Targets differ for chronic respiratory disease.</div></details>
    <div class="callout">Athletes may have resting HRs in the 40s; always interpret vitals together with the patient.</div>
  </div>
</Base>
